# Environment variables for GROWUPHOST.
#
# `.env` IS COMMITTED IN THIS REPO, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. It contains only the
# three values below — a project ref, a URL, and a *publishable* key. Vite inlines
# every `VITE_`-prefixed value into the client bundle at build time, so the
# publishable key is public the moment the site is deployed; hiding it in the repo
# would protect nothing while breaking `npm run dev` and `vite build` for anyone
# who clones. Row-level security, not key secrecy, is what protects the data.
#
# THE SERVICE-ROLE KEY IS THE OPPOSITE and must never be written to a tracked
# file. It bypasses RLS entirely. Set it only in the hosting provider's
# environment (Lovable / Cloudflare), where `src/integrations/supabase/
# client.server.ts` reads it via `process.env`.

# --- Client + SSR (safe to commit; read by src/integrations/supabase/client.ts) ---
# Both spellings are needed: `VITE_*` for the browser bundle, bare for the SSR
# process, because `import.meta.env` is not populated in the Node/Worker runtime.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-ref>"
SUPABASE_URL="https://<project-ref>.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_..."
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="<project-ref>"

# --- Server only (NEVER commit; set in the hosting dashboard) ---
# Read by src/integrations/supabase/client.server.ts for RLS-bypassing admin work.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="sb_secret_..."
